      "content": "helplines don't pay rent or bring my life back. everyone just says \"it gets better\" or \"stay strong\" but they don't get it. they aren't the ones staring at a wall in a dark room wondering why they even bothered to be a good person. it feels like the world is just telling me to keep suffering for a sense of morality that doesn't even exist in reality. if the cost of being decent is this much misery, maybe the cost was just too high. maybe there really isn't a way back from this.",
